{"seconds": 76.2, "exit": 0, "final": "After Qxf4, White can play **Bxf4** (bishop on d2 takes), and the position is roughly equal. But wait\u2014the main point is that most of Black's moves lose the queen:\n- Qxg2+ allows Bxg2 or Nxg2 winning the queen\n- Qg3+ allows Kxg3 winning the queen  \n- Qxf4 trades queens after Bxf4\n\nSo **Nf4** is clearly the best move. It forces Black into a losing position because:\n1. The queen cannot find safety\n2. Most moves either lose the queen outright or lead to a won endgame for White\n\nThe main line would be: **1. Nf4 Qg3+ 2. Kxg3**, winning the queen.\n\n**Best move:** Nf4\n\n**Main line:** Nf4 Qg3+ Kxg3 (winning the queen), or if Qxg2+ then Bxg2 (winning the queen), or if Qxf4 then Bxf4 (roughly equal but better than the current position).\n\n**Motif:** fork (the knight forks the king and queen's escape squares, forcing the queen into danger)\n\n**Coaching note:** After Nf4, Black's queen has no safe square. Every check (Qg3+, Qh4+, Qg1+) or capture (Qxg2+, Qxf4) either loses the queen immediately or walks into a devastating attack. When your opponent's queen is on the rim, look for knight moves that cut off escape routes.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Nf4\", \"line\": [\"Nf4\", \"Qg3+\", \"Kxg3\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"attraction\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r3k1nr/p2b1ppp/2p5/3pb3/4P3/P4B2/1PPBNKPq/R2Q1R2 w kq - 1 20"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r3k1nr/p2b1ppp/2p5/3pb3/4P3/P4B2/1PPBNKPq/R2Q1R2 w kq - 1 20"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r3k1nr/p2b1ppp/2p5/3pb3/4P3/P4B2/1PPBNKPq/R2Q1R2 w kq - 1 20"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3k1nr/p2b1ppp/2p5/3pb3/4P3/P4B2/1PPBNKPq/R2Q1R2 w kq - 1 20", "move": "Nf4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3k1nr/p2b1ppp/2p5/3pb3/4P3/P4B2/1PPBNKPq/R2Q1R2 w kq - 1 20", "move": "exd5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes